NAME
     mount - attach a file system

SYNOPSIS
     mount [-t TYPE] [-o OPTIONS] [-r|-w] [--bind] SOURCE TARGET
     mount

DESCRIPTION
     mount attaches SOURCE at TARGET. With no arguments it prints what
     is mounted. The types are ext4, tmpfs, ramfs, procfs, devfs, sysfs
     and overlay; --bind attaches a directory somewhere else as well.

     In a mount namespace this changes only that namespace's table, and
     a container may mount only the harmless types, always nodev and
     nosuid.

OPTIONS
     -t TYPE      the file system type
     -o OPTIONS   ro, rw, nodev, nosuid, noexec, sync, data=ordered,
                  data=journal, size=N, lowerdir=, upperdir=, workdir=
     -r, -w       read-only or read-write
     --bind       attach a directory at a second place

SEE ALSO
     umount(1), df(1), losetup(8), fstab(5)
